# 7. What Can We Do Using SQL?

SQL can be used for several types of operations.

Imagine we have this table:

### Students

| student_id | name | age | department |
| ---------: | ---- | --: | ---------- |
|        101 | Ravi |  20 | CSE        |
|        102 | Sita |  21 | ECE        |
|        103 | Arun |  20 | CSE        |

We may want to:

### Create a table

> "Create a table called students."

### Insert data

> "Add Ravi to the students table."

### Read data

> "Show all students."

### Search data

> "Show only CSE students."

### Update data

> "Change Ravi's age."

### Delete data

> "Remove a student."

All of these operations can be performed using SQL.

